    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="22">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 22</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="98" ed="#liebermann"/>LXVI. Gif ðin geneat stalie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.11"/> ⁊ losie ðe, gif ðu hæbbe byrgean<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.12"/>, mana þone þæs angyldes; gif he næbbe, gyld ðu þæt angylde, ⁊ ne sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.13"/> him no<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.14-2"/> ðy ðingodre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="98" ed="#liebermann"/>LXVI. [G]if þin geneat stalie ⁊ losie ðe, gif þu habbe bergan, manna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.1-2"/> ðone þæs angeldes; gif he næbbe, geld þu þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> angelde, ⁊ ne sie hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> no ðy ðingodre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="98" ed="#liebermann"/>LXVI. Gif þin geneat stalige ⁊ losige ðe, gif þu hæbbe byrgan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.8"/>, mana ðone ðæs angyldes; gif he næbbe, gild þu þæt angylde, ⁊ ne sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.9"/> him no<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.2"/> ðe geðingrode.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.10"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="99" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe mannes geneat stalige. Gyf ðin geneat stalie ⁊ losig<hi rend="italic">e</hi> ðe, gyf ðu hæbbe borgas, mana ðone ðæs angyldas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.1"/>; gyf he næbbe, gyld ðu þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> angylde, ⁊ ne sy him na þe g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>ðingodre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="22" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.star"/><pb n="99" ed="#liebermann"/>Si tuus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.14"/> geneat (id est [colonus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.15"/> uel] uillanus) furetur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.16"/> et amittatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.17"/> tibi, si habeas plegium, admone eum de angildo.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.18"/> Si non habeas, redde tu angelde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.19"/>; et non sit ei in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_22.lnote.oe.20"/> aliquo remissius.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="42" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðam þe mannes geneat stalige.] Gif ðin geneat stalie ⁊ losie ðe, gif ðu hæbbe byrgean<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Ine_22.attnote.fn.13"/>, mana þone þæs angyldes; gif he næbbe, gyld ðu þæt angylde, ⁊ ne sie him no ðy ðingodre<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Ine_22.attnote.fn.14"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="21" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="386" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXVI} Gif ðin geneat stalie ⁊ losie ðe, gif ðu hæbbe byrgean, mana þone þæs angyldes, Gif he næbbe, gyld ðu þæt angylde, ⁊ ne sie him no ðy ðingodre.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="99" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn dein Gefolgsmann (Hausgenosse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_22.lnote.de.1"/>) stiehlt und dir entkommt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_22.lnote.de.2"/>, mahne, falls du einen Bürgen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_22.lnote.de.3"/> [für ihn] hast, diesen um den Ersatz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_22.lnote.de.4"/> [für das Gestohlene]; wenn jener<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_22.lnote.de.5"/> [Dieb] keinen [Bürgen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_22.lnote.de.6"/>] hat, so zahle du den Ersatz; jedoch darum sei für jenen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_22.lnote.de.7"/> [die Schuld] nimmer gesühnter.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If your retainer (household member) steals and escapes from you, then, if you have a surety [for him], demand the compensation [for what was stolen] from him; if that [thief] has no [surety], pay the compensation yourself; but [the guilt] is not on that account any the more atoned for him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="43" ed="#attenborough"/>If a member of your household commits a theft and escapes from you, and if you have a surety [for the thief], you shall claim the value of the stolen property from him. If the thief has no surety, you shall pay the value [of the property], but he shall not thereby become immune from punishment.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="402" ed="#whitelock"/>If your <hi rend="italic">geneat</hi> steals and escapes from you, if you have a surety, demand the compensation from him; if he has no surety, pay you the compensation, and he is not to be any nearer a settlement on that account.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="387" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a member of your household steals and runs away, if you have [one who stands] surety [for him], claim from him the single value [of the stolen goods]. If [the thief] does not have [one who stands surety], you pay the single value, but [the thief] is not thus released from culpability.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:App-AGu_3">App AGu 3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="387"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_19">Ine 19</ref> <quote>The geneat of this clause appears to be of lower standing than the king's geneat of §19.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="387"><label>more akin to</label> <ref target="clause:Rect_2">Rect 2</ref> <quote>This figure may be more akin to the geneat described in §2 of Rectitudines Singularum Personarum</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="383"><ref target="clause:Ine_19">Ine 19</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Cap.</hi> 22 <hi rend="italic">steht auch in App. ad Aelfr. et Guthr. foedus</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. o. S.</hi> 93*), <hi rend="italic">c.</hi> 3.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cap. 22 also occurs in App. ad Aelfr. et Guthr. foedus (see above p. 93*), c. 3.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quis <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quis R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">col. uel <hi rend="italic">nicht in Lond App. A Gu., nachgetragen Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">col. uel not in Lond App. A Gu., added later Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">furatus fuerit <hi rend="italic">M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">furatus fuerit M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> amittas eum <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> am. ti. <hi rend="italic">übrige;</hi> aufugiat <hi rend="italic">App. A Gu.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; amittas eum instead of am. ti. the others; aufugiat App. A Gu.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lde <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lde T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> angildum <hi rend="italic">übrige; App. A Gu.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; angildum the others; App. A Gu.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">rem. in al. <hi rend="italic">App. A Gu.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rem. in al. App. A Gu.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> -gean</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to -gean</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> -godre</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read -godre</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">stalige ⁊ losige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">stalige ⁊ losige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">borgas <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">borgas Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.oe.14-2" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">na ðe geþingodre <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">na ðe geþingodre Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Bauer’ Q. Aber an eines solchen Vieh oder Vorrat hätte sich der Herr halten können, ohne dass es Bürgen bedurfte. Vermutlich meint Ine landloses Gesinde; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Gefolge 19</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Peasant’ Q. But the lord could have recovered from such a man’s cattle or stores without needing sureties. Ine presumably means landless household servants; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Gefolge 19</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Bürgschaft 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Bürgschaft 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Herr schiebt sich zwischen landlosen Angeklagten vom Gefolge und Volksgericht ein</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The lord interposes himself between the landless accused member of his retinue and the folk-court</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Busse für Verletzten und Strafe trifft den Dieb (<hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Abfindung 4); nur für den Wert des Gestohlenen trägt der Herr (bzw. der Bürge) Haftung (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7d), so auch II As 19 der des Unfreien. So Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 41</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Compensation to the injured party and the fine fall upon the thief (<hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Abfindung 4); the lord (or the surety) is liable (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7d) only for the value of what was stolen, as in II As 19 the lord of the unfree man is too. So Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 41</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q bleibt bei 2. Person, was den Sinn nicht ändert: denselben Bürgen ‘hat’ der Herr, um sich zu sichern, und der Mann, um von ihm bei Herrensuche verbürgt zu werden</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q keeps the 2nd person, which does not alter the sense: the lord ‘has’ the same surety in order to secure himself, and the man in order to be vouched for by him when seeking a lord</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘kein Vermögen zum Ersatz’; es ist dasselbe Objekt wie zum Ggsatz <hi rend="italic">hæbbe</hi> vorher hinzuzudenken. Der vermögenslose Bürge fiele in Schuldknechtschaft</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘no means to make restitution’; the same object is to be supplied as with the contrasting <hi rend="italic">hæbbe</hi> before. A surety without means would fall into debt-bondage</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_22.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘mehr abgedungen’ etymologisch näher Schmid</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Schmid’s ‘more stipulated’ is etymologically closer</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_22.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>byrgean</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">borgas</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_22.attnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>ðingodre</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">geðingodre</hi>. B, H.</seg></note>
      </div>
